# Frontend Design

When building widgets, screens, or UI flows:

## Design Direction

- [ ] Pick one clear aesthetic (minimal, refined, playful, editorial, etc.) and commit to it
- [ ] Define purpose, audience, and what makes this UI memorable
- [ ] Match implementation complexity to the vision (maximalist → rich motion; minimal → precision spacing)

## Typography & Theme

- [ ] Use `ThemeData` / `TextTheme` with clear hierarchy — not flat system defaults only
- [ ] Pair display + body fonts intentionally; avoid overused defaults (Roboto-only, Space Grotesk everywhere)
- [ ] Use `ColorScheme` and project constants (`primaryColor`, `theme.dart`) for a cohesive palette
- [ ] Dominant color + sharp accents; avoid timid evenly-distributed palettes

## Layout & Depth

- [ ] Use intentional spatial composition — asymmetry, overlap, or generous whitespace
- [ ] Scrollable content uses opaque widgets (`OpaqueGroupedSection`); chrome uses glass per `theme.dart`
- [ ] Add depth via gradients, shadows, transparency — not flat solid fills by default

## Motion & Feedback

- [ ] One high-impact entrance or transition beats scattered micro-animations
- [ ] Use `AnimatedSwitcher`, `Hero`, implicit/explicit animations where they reinforce the aesthetic
- [ ] Gestures, focus, and tap states feel responsive

## Avoid

- [ ] Purple-on-white gradient clichés and cookie-cutter component patterns
- [ ] Generic layouts that could belong to any app
- [ ] Copying the same font/palette across unrelated screens
